# fstack Model Roles

This file configures which models flash-mode uses for different types of work.
Copy this to `~/.cursor/rules/fstack-models.mdc` and customize.

## Investigation
Model: claude-sonnet
Use for: Understanding existing code, tracing behavior, /how-ui, /why-this-design

## Implementation
Model: claude-sonnet
Use for: Writing and modifying code, Figma-to-code, bug fixes

## Judgment
Model: claude-opus
Use for: Design decisions, architecture choices, complex tradeoffs

## Review
Models: claude-opus, claude-sonnet
Use for: Multi-perspective critique, code review, accessibility audit

## Prose
Model: claude-opus
Use for: UX copy, documentation, PR descriptions, /unslop

## Notes

- To use the chat's current model, set to `auto` or `inherit-parent`
- Review role accepts multiple models for diverse perspectives
- Run `/setup-fstack` to auto-detect your available models
- Adjust based on your Cursor subscription and budget
